{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01FPA8vpnBdRgcjAjLh59U2w","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user wants me to define three tiers (best/median/worst) for a Dream simulation of this research project. Let me analyze the current state carefully.\n\nCurrent state:\n- Dual-contribution framing: Likert Blindspot + per-axis confound structure\n- Strong evidence already: BT 63-77% across axes, 7 Likert methods all NS, bootstrap attenuation curve, GEE decomposition, NLI ablation reversal, Claude negative control\n- Pending: Llama-70B (downloading), 100-point fine-grained Likert ablation\n- Current score: 3.5, targeting 4.0\n\n\n- Venue: EMNLP 2026 Main\n\nTwo critical experiments will shape the outcome tiers. First, whether Llama-70B exhibits the same bias pattern across all three target architectures, establishing generalizability beyond Claude. Second, the 100-point Likert ablation—if it remains non-significant, that strengthens the core Blindspot claim that scale granularity doesn't overcome the measurement mode problem; if it shows significance, that weakens the framing. The best case would have Llama replicating the bias while the fine-grained scale still misses it, solidifying both the architectural consistency and the measurement limitation argument.\n\nIn a median scenario, Llama might show mixed results across dimensions or the Likert scale could detect marginal effects like verbosity bias, requiring some claim softening but still preserving the dual-contribution story. The worst case would be Llama showing no bias pattern while the 100-point scale suddenly detects it, which would flip the entire narrative from a measurement mode problem to a scale granularity issue and demand a complete reframing.\n\nNow I'm setting concrete thresholds for each outcome tier—Llama's formality and verbosity detection rates, effect sizes from the Likert scale, and an overall venue score target that tracks how well the story holds together. I'm anchoring these against existing baseline data like GPT-4o's 63% formality rate and Qwen's 66%, so I can calibrate what counts as strong, marginal, or null results. Now I'm looking at the performance metrics across different scales and judge types—the 100-point Likert scale shows much tighter effect sizes across the board compared to the binary choice, which suggests the Blindspot might be more about scale granularity than the underlying bias mechanism itself. The key questions are whether Llama generalizes these findings and whether the finer scale actually breaks the core claim, so I should focus the analysis on those two dimensions before moving forward with the YAML structure.\n\nWriting YAML config... _ranges, I should include:\n- llama_bt_formality\n- llama_bt_verbosity  \n- llama_likert_formality_d\n- llama_likert_verbosity_d\n- likert_100pt_formality_d\n- likert_100pt_verbosity_d\n- n_biased_judges (out of 3 target)\n- mf1_layers_holding (out of 5)\n\nActually, looking at the paper framing more carefully:\n\nThe \"key question\" stated is: \"does the dual-contribution framing + agnostic stance push above 3.5? Best case: Llama shows bias + 100-point Likert NS + bootstrap confirms attenuation. Worst case: Llama no bias + 100-point Likert detects bias.\"\n\nSo the user already has intuitions about best/worst.\n\nNow I need to nail down the exact numbers and medians. The interesting middle ground is when Llama catches bias on one axis but not the other—that actually strengthens the narrative by showing the confound structure varies per-dimension. If the 100-point scale only picks up verbosity bias, I can reframe it as \"scale granularity partially resolves the blindspot but doesn't eliminate it.\" For the worst case where Llama misses bias entirely but the 100-point scale catches it, the story shifts from \"mode sensitivity\" to \"scale sensitivity\"—the architecture-dependent and scale-dependent nature of style bias becomes the core finding, with the confound decomposition as the primary contribution.\n\nThe per-axis confound structure itself is already solid across GPT-4o and Qwen3-32B, so even in worst case, that backbone holds. The GEE decomposition showing verbosity as pure confound, formality as conditional, and register as originality-dominated is established. Now I need to finalize the YAML with precise numbers.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":33480,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":33480},"output_tokens":28,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"067154de-4caf-4fba-a982-07a085239900","uuid":"f9f06cce-58eb-47ab-bf09-e7048bdaf342"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01FPA8vpnBdRgcjAjLh59U2w","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"```yaml\ntiers:\n  best:\n    meaning: \"所有待验证假设成立：第三架构复现 bias + 细粒度 Likert 仍失灵 → dual-contribution 完整成立，冲 4.0\"\n    key_assumptions:\n      - \"Llama-70B 在 formality 和 verbosity 上均检测到显著 bias（BT ≥60%，p<0.05）\"\n      - \"100-point Likert 在所有 axis 上仍 NS（d<0.10）→ Blindspot 是 measurement mode 问题，非 scale granularity\"\n      - \"Llama GEE 复现三轴 confound 结构（verbosity pure / formality conditional / register originality-dominated）\"\n      - \"MF1 五层防御全部成立（Llama 作为第 5 层 = 三独立架构一致）\"\n    number_ranges:\n      llama_bt_formality: [0.60, 0.70]\n      llama_bt_verbosity: [0.68, 0.82]\n      llama_likert_formality_d: [-0.05, 0.05]\n      llama_likert_verbosity_d: [-0.05, 0.15]\n      likert_100pt_formality_d: [-0.05, 0.08]\n      likert_100pt_verbosity_d: [0.00, 0.10]\n      likert_100pt_formality_p: [0.15, 1.0]\n      likert_100pt_verbosity_p: [0.10, 1.0]\n      n_biased_target_judges: [3, 3]\n      mf1_layers_holding: [5, 5]\n    narrative_direction: >\n      原始 D059 framing 完全成立，无需调整。Title claim \"Likert Blindspot\" 以三架构 × 三基准 × 三轴验证。\n      100-point Likert NS 作为 §5 的 killer evidence：即使 100 级量表也检测不到 BT 63-77% 的 bias，\n      measurement mode > scale granularity 结论牢固。Per-axis confound structure 跨三架构复现 →\n      prescriptive guidance 有三重独立验证。Agnostic stance 保守但 bootstrap curve + 100pt NS 强烈\n      倾向 attenuation 解释。预期 reviewer score 4.0-4.5。\n\n  median:\n    meaning: \"Llama 部分复现（一轴 sig 一轴 NS）或 100-point Likert 在 verbosity 出现 marginal signal → 需调整 claim 强度但核心故事成立\"\n    key_assumptions:\n      - \"Llama-70B verbosity 显著（BT 60-70%）但 formality NS 或 marginal（BT 53-58%）\"\n      - \"或：Llama 两轴均显著，但 100-point Likert verbosity 出现 marginal signal（d=0.15-0.25, p=0.03-0.10）\"\n      - \"Per-axis confound structure 在 Llama 上基本复现（至少 verbosity pure pattern 成立）\"\n      - \"MF1 防御 4/5 层成立（Llama 层部分成立或需降级为 qualitative evidence）\"\n    number_ranges:\n      llama_bt_formality: [0.52, 0.60]\n      llama_bt_verbosity: [0.60, 0.72]\n      llama_likert_formality_d: [-0.05, 0.10]\n      llama_likert_verbosity_d: [0.00, 0.20]\n      likert_100pt_formality_d: [-0.05, 0.12]\n      likert_100pt_verbosity_d: [0.10, 0.25]\n      likert_100pt_formality_p: [0.08, 1.0]\n      likert_100pt_verbosity_p: [0.03, 0.15]\n      n_biased_target_judges: [2, 3]\n      mf1_layers_holding: [4, 5]\n    narrative_direction: >\n      两种 median 子场景需不同调整：\n      (A) Llama formality NS：将 C3 从 \"3 judges biased\" 调整为 \"2/3 judges biased, architecture-dependent \n      susceptibility\"，Llama formality 作为 partial negative control 增加 nuance。Verbosity 仍有三架构支撑。\n      Formality claim 降为 \"GPT-4o/Qwen3 specific\"。\n      (B) 100-point Likert verbosity marginal：Blindspot 从 \"categorical\" 调整为 \"graduated\" —— \n      \"fine-grained Likert partially mitigates but does not eliminate the Blindspot; \n      measurement mode remains the dominant factor (BT d_equivalent=0.77 vs Likert-100 d=0.20)\"。\n      两种情况下 per-axis confound structure (C2b) 不受影响，作为 co-primary 贡献撑住 novelty。\n      需在 §6 Limitations 增加 1-2 段。预期 reviewer score 3.5-4.0，Findings 保底。\n\n  worst:\n    meaning: \"Llama 无 bias（类似 Claude）且 100-point Likert 检测到 verbosity bias → 核心 Blindspot claim 被削弱，需 reframe\"\n    key_assumptions:\n      - \"Llama-70B 两轴均 NS（BT <55%，类似 Claude pattern）→ 只有 2/4 judges biased\"\n      - \"100-point Likert verbosity 显著（d>0.25, p<0.05）→ Blindspot 部分是 scale granularity 而非 pure mode difference\"\n      - \"Per-axis confound structure 仍成立（GPT-4o + Qwen3-32B 数据不变）\"\n      - \"Formality 100-point Likert 仍 NS（formality effect size 本就较小，即使 100-point 也检测不到）\"\n    number_ranges:\n      llama_bt_formality: [0.48, 0.55]\n      llama_bt_verbosity: [0.48, 0.56]\n      llama_likert_formality_d: [-0.05, 0.05]\n      llama_likert_verbosity_d: [-0.10, 0.10]\n      likert_100pt_formality_d: [-0.05, 0.10]\n      likert_100pt_verbosity_d: [0.25, 0.40]\n      likert_100pt_formality_p: [0.10, 1.0]\n      likert_100pt_verbosity_p: [0.001, 0.05]\n      n_biased_target_judges: [2, 2]\n      mf1_layers_holding: [3, 4]\n    narrative_direction: >\n      Reframe 策略（仍冲 EMNLP Main）：\n      (1) 升级 C2b 为 sole primary：Per-axis confound structure 成为论文核心贡献。Title 改为 \n      \"When Style Bias Hides in Plain Sight: Per-Axis Confound Decomposition for LLM Judge Auditing\"。\n      (2) Blindspot 降为 conditional finding：Blindspot 仅对 moderate-effect axes（formality, d_BT≈0.63-0.67）\n      成立；strong-effect axes（verbosity, d_BT≈0.77）可被 fine-grained Likert 部分检测到。\n      Reframe 为 \"effect-size-dependent measurement sensitivity\" —— 更 nuanced，实际更有学术价值。\n      (3) Judge susceptibility 成为 empirical contribution：2/4 judges biased（GPT-4o, Qwen3）vs \n      2/4 unbiased（Claude, Llama）→ \"CSD as diagnostic tool reveals which architectures are susceptible\"，\n      50/50 split 比 3/4 实际更有 practical value（不是所有 judge 都有 bias）。\n      (4) Bootstrap attenuation curve 仍成立：formality d≈0 是 definitive，不受 100-point Likert \n      verbosity 结果影响（不同 axis）。\n      风险：novelty 天花板降低（confound decomposition 单挑大梁），但统计方法论深度 + honest framing \n      仍足以支撑 EMNLP Main。预期 reviewer score 3.0-3.5，需要强 rebuttal 冲 Findings。\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":33480,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":33480},"output_tokens":28,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"067154de-4caf-4fba-a982-07a085239900","uuid":"6e2fda01-e8f5-4c98-a3ef-b66d2130d337"}
